---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="About" description={`About ${site.name} — ${site.tagline}`}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-(--container-reading) px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">About</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">{site.location}</p>

    <!-- Plain prose, deliberately. Recruiters and their screening tools both
         need to parse this, and specifics land harder than adjectives. -->
    <div class="prose-portfolio mt-8">
      <p>
        I'm the Operations Technology Manager at RMH3 Dental Supply. I build and run the
        software the business depends on — order intake across five sales channels,
        inventory sync, automated repricing, and the integrations that keep QuickBooks
        and the warehouse in agreement. The catalog is north of 20,000 SKUs, and daily
        orders went from about 200 to 400 while I've been there.
      </p>
      <p>
        Almost everything I've built started as something a person was doing by hand.
        Repricing was a spreadsheet someone updated every morning. The inventory sync
        exists because two systems disagreed and somebody had to reconcile them at the
        end of every day. Those are the problems I like — the ones where the fix has to
        survive contact with people actually using it, and where being subtly wrong is
        worse than being obviously broken.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before this I trained as a Software Developer in Test at CYDEO, which is where
        the testing habits came from: Selenium, Cucumber, REST Assured, and a strong
        preference for automating anything I'd otherwise have to check twice. I studied
        Computer Science at George Mason University.
      </p>
      <p>
        The projects here are the ones worth explaining. Each one says what the problem
        actually was, what was non-obvious about the approach, and what came out of it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-faint">
      What I work with
    </h2>
    <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {[
        { k: 'Languages', v: 'Java, Python, JavaScript/TypeScript, SQL' },
        { k: 'Backend & data', v: 'Flask, REST APIs, PostgreSQL, Oracle, MySQL, JDBC' },
        { k: 'Testing', v: 'Selenium, Cucumber, REST Assured, JUnit, TestNG, PyTest, Postman' },
        { k: 'Ops', v: 'Git, CI/CD, Jenkins, GitHub Actions, Jira' },
      ].map((row) => (
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface p-4">
          <dt class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-faint">{row.k}</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink">{row.v}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      {site.resumeUrl && (
        <a
          href={site.resumeUrl}
          class="rounded-lg border border-border px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-ink transition-colors hover:border-border-strong"
        >
          Résumé (PDF)
        </a>
      )}
      <a
        href="/contact"
        class="rounded-lg bg-accent px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-accent-ink transition-colors hover:bg-accent-hover"
      >
        Get in touch
      </a>
      <a
        href={site.links.github}
        rel="noopener"
        class="rounded-lg border border-border px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-ink transition-colors hover:border-border-strong"
      >
        GitHub
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
